    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Square the difference",
        "body": "Square both sides of $x-y=10$:\n$$x^2-2xy+y^2=100.$$\nSince $xy=5$, $2xy=10$, so $x^2+y^2=100+10=110$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 110**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Find $x$ and $y$",
        "body": "From $x=y+10$: $(y+10)y=5$, so $y^2+10y-5=0$ and $y=-5\\pm\\sqrt{30}$, $x=5\\pm\\sqrt{30}$ (same sign choice).\n\nThen $x^2+y^2=(5+\\sqrt{30})^2+(-5+\\sqrt{30})^2 = (55+10\\sqrt{30})+(55-10\\sqrt{30})=110$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 110**"
      }
    ],
